    [Performance][GDN][Main] Reduce QKV layout copies for FLA attention (#18723)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Reduce unnecessary QKV layout copies in Gated DeltaNet attention:
    - Use head-first convolution output for prefill and reuse contiguous
    BNSD views on A5.
    - Process decode and prefill convolution separately in ordinary mixed
    batches.
    - Avoid intermediate QKV concatenation in ordinary and speculative
    decode.
    - Make inputs contiguous before fallback L2 normalization to support
    head-first and sliced layouts.
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No API or configuration changes. This optimizes internal tensor layout
    handling while preserving attention behavior.
    ### How was this patch tested?
    Added and updated regression tests covering QKV layouts, mixed batches,
    ordinary and speculative decode, and multi-head normalization fallback:
    - tests/ut/ops/test_gdn.py
    - tests/ut/ops/test_gdn_decode_qkv.py
    - tests/ut/ops/test_gdn_layout.py
    - tests/ut/ops/test_gdn_mixed_batch.py
    Ruff lint, formatting, and git diff --check passed. Python syntax checks
    passed before formatting.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
